\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Turn Back, O man, forswear
\par thy foolish ways;
\par Old now is earth, and none may
\par count her days,
\par Yet thou, her child, whose head is 
\par crowned with flame,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Still wilt not hear thine inner
\par God proclaim:
\par Turn Back, O man, forswear
\par thy foolish ways.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Earth might be fair and all 
\par men glad and wise,
\par Age after age their tragic 
\par empires rise,
\par Built while they dream, and in
\par that dreaming weep:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Would man but wake from out 
\par his haunted sleep,
\par Earth might be fair and all 
\par men glad and wise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Earth shall be fair, and all
\par her people one:
\par Nor till that hour shall God's 
\par whole will be done;
\par Now, even now, once more
\par thou earth to sky,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Peals forth in joy man's old
\par undaunted cry:
\par Earth shall be fair, and all
\par her folk be one.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

